---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { supabaseUrl } from "../lib/supabase-public";
const termsPreview = `${supabaseUrl}/storage/v1/object/public/materuni-images/waterfall_image/1791601414950-ew7ak42gjka.jpg`;
---
<SiteLayout title="Booking Terms & Conditions | Materuni Hosts" description="Review Materuni Hosts booking requests, per-person prices, availability, payment arrangements, transport and practical conditions before your visit." preloadImage={termsPreview}>
<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow" data-i18n="terms_eyebrow">BEFORE YOU BOOK</span><h1 data-i18n="terms_title">Simple, clear booking terms.</h1><p data-i18n="terms_intro">What to expect when planning a Materuni experience with a local host.</p></section>
<section class="section legal-copy">
  <h2>Booking requests & confirmation</h2>
  <p>Submitting the website form sends a booking request; it does not create a confirmed reservation. A local host will check the requested date, experience and group details, then confirm availability and arrangements with you before the booking is final.</p>
  <h2>Experience prices & inclusions</h2>
  <p>Published experience prices are shown per person in US dollars. Please review the individual experience page for the current description, inclusions and exclusions. Any final price or adjustment will be confirmed by your host before you agree to proceed.</p>
  <h2>Transport & pickup</h2>
  <p>Transport to and from Materuni is not included unless it is specifically confirmed as part of your arrangements. You may request pickup from Moshi, Kilimanjaro International Airport (KIA), Arusha or another location. Availability and any separate transport quote will be confirmed by your host before you accept it.</p>
  <h2>Payment arrangements</h2>
  <p>No payment is taken when you submit a website booking request. Payment timing and available payment methods will be explained by your host after the experience details and availability have been confirmed. Please rely on the payment instructions provided for your specific booking.</p>
  <h2>Changes, cancellations & refunds</h2>
  <p>Any applicable change, cancellation or refund arrangements will be communicated by your host and agreed with you as part of the booking confirmation. If you need to change your plans, contact Materuni Hosts as early as possible using the details below.</p>
  <h2>Weather, trail conditions & safety</h2>
  <p>Some experiences include walking on uneven, wet or sloping forest paths. We recommend sturdy walking shoes with good grip and a light rain layer. Routes and activities may need to be adjusted if local weather or trail conditions affect safe access; your host will discuss the available arrangements with you.</p>
  <h2>Health, dietary needs & accessibility</h2>
  <p>Please tell your host in advance about dietary requirements, allergies, mobility considerations or other practical needs that may affect your experience. The host can then discuss the experience details and whether the requested arrangements are suitable.</p>
  <h2>Children & family visits</h2>
  <p>Families are welcome to enquire about suitable experiences. Please share the ages of children in your group and your preferred activities so your host can discuss the route, conditions and supervision needs before confirming.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For booking questions, contact <a href="mailto:hello@materunihosts.com">hello@materunihosts.com</a> or WhatsApp <a href="https://wa.me/255612068540">+255 612 068 540</a>.</p>
  <p class="muted legal-updated">Last updated: 1 November 2026.</p>
</section>
</SiteLayout>
